## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to translate CKNE (Customer Key Need Engagement) into concrete cache behavior, tiering strategies, and fairness mechanisms under SLA constraints, while implementing a time-based rebalancing loop. It combines practical edge cache architecture with state management and real-time optimization.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-to-cache allocation mapping
- Tier promotion/demotion logic
- Minute-by-minute rebalancing with SLA guarantees
- Weighted eviction policy integration (LRU with CKNE weights)

## Code Example

```javascript
function adjustQuotas(tenants, ckneMap, totalSlots) {
  // Compute per-tenant target slots based on CKNE
  const weights = tenants.map(t => Math.max(0.01, ckneMap[t] ?? 0));
  const weightSum = weights.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);

  // Allocate baseline + CKNE-proportional slots
  const baselineSlots = Math.floor(totalSlots * 0.3 / tenants.length);
  const dynamicSlots = totalSlots * 0.7;

  return tenants.map((tenant, i) => ({
    tenant,
    totalSlots: baselineSlots + Math.floor(dynamicSlots * weights[i] / weightSum),
    hotTTL: 60 * (1 + ckneMap[tenant]), // 1-2 minutes based on CKNE
    warmTTL: 300 * (1 + ckneMap[tenant] * 2), // 5-15 minutes
    coldTTL: 1800 * (1 + ckneMap[tenant] * 3) // 30-90 minutes
  }));
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Edge compute with CKNE requires concrete scheduling strategies, policy definitions, and measurable SLAs under dynamic workloads.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-budget mapping: slots, memory, and concurrency limits per tenant
- Minute-by-minute scheduler: preemption rules, reallocation, and SLA guarantees
- Edge runtimes and observability: lightweight workers, per-tenant state, and metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal pseudo-scheduler snippet
function decideSlotAllocation(state, ckne) {
  // ckne in [0,1], returns slot budget for tenant
  // higher ckne => more slots
  const base = state.baseSlots;
  const ramp = Math.max(0.0, Math.min(1.0, ckne));
  return Math.floor(base * (0.5 + ramp * 0.5));
}
```

